      "exp_en": "D is correct — the practitioner's income is not an element of informed consent. Informed consent means the patient agrees to treatment and understands the nature of the proposed procedure, alternatives, consequences of not having treatment, possible risks, and expected results. The actual consent is the meaningful dialogue between practitioner and patient; a signed form is only evidence of that consent. Written consent is especially important for procedures that may cause bruising, such as cupping, gua sha, or direct moxibustion.",
      "exp_hant": "D 正確——執業者的收入不是知情同意的要素。知情同意是指病人同意治療，並理解擬議程序的性質、替代方案、不治療的後果、可能的風險與預期結果。真正的同意是執業者與病人之間有意義的對話；簽署的表單只是該同意的「證據」。對於可能造成瘀傷的程序（如拔罐、刮痧或直接灸），取得書面同意尤其重要。"
